&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;New page&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div&gt;The '''Configuration Widget''' displays a configuration table that is used to show property settings to the user.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The widget color controls the color of the configuration table's border.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
== Settings ==&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
The following settings are available specifically for Configuration Widgets.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
{| {{Table}}&lt;br /&gt;
{{Tablehead|Setting|Description}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{HeadingSetting|'''Configuration&amp;amp;nbsp;Settings'''}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Setting|'''Title column fraction'''|Determines what fraction of the full width of the table is used for the setting titles. A vertical line is rendered in between the title column and value column in the table.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Setting|'''Show script variable column'''|Used by the [[Script Editor]] to indicate that a third column be shown for variable name entry.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Setting|'''Line color'''|If checked, specifies the color of the border lines inside the configuration table, overriding the default color given by the average of 50% gray and the window frame color given by the &amp;lt;code&amp;gt;$windowFrameColor&amp;lt;/code&amp;gt; system variable.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|-&lt;br /&gt;
{{Setting|'''Background color'''|Specifies the background color for the configuration table.}}&lt;br /&gt;
|}&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
